Z||000000||Nightwing||08-25-2000||04:38 PM||||I was talking to a "gearhead" said a few yrs back he had seen a fiero(84) with the motor put in 'north/south'. Instead of 'east/west'. If that makes sense ... But he said it made so much more room for the twin turbos that were set up off the sides. he said the lift gate had a serious mod. they had section off the middle of the deck lid & raised it 4 1/2 inches & vented it. this would be something i am serious about doing. Think it would be the that "one-of-a-kinda-idea" that would set it apart from the rest.  One other qst anyone ever seen a "drop box" used to mate the tranny to the engine ?||||reg||3
